The fee payer change (16 October 2026, not signed by a verifier; ZOLANA.md section 5). A fee key
of the proposing seat pays every fee and rent, and the group key is a readonly signer, so the
group key never pays. The rules and the template of the checker change, and the manifest below
marks each changed file `modified`:
- src/pins.rs: a fourth pin, the payer (129 bytes on the wire). Pins::devnet takes it.
- src/intent.rs: Shield (shown to people as Add SOL) has a blockhash in place of a nonce, and uses
  no nonce: the payer signs it alone.
- src/template.rs: the payer is the first account and the fee payer of every message. The group
  key is a readonly signer: nonce authority, base of the nonce account (the payer funds it), owner
  of the registry record, and owner signer of `transact` (after the nullifier accounts, before the
  settlement accounts, as programs/shielded-pool transact/account.rs and the SDK sponsor mode
  list it). Shield lists the payer as the depositor and has no group account. `signer_count` is 2
  (1 for Shield). `compile` refuses a payer that is the group key.
- src/rule.rs, src/check.rs, src/rules_ix.rs: `fee-payer-not-group` is `fee-payer-not-payer`
  (the first account is the payer of the proposal). New: `payer-is-group` (the group key is never
  the payer) and `group-debit` (no System Transfer, CreateAccount, CreateAccountWithSeed or
  TransferWithSeed has the group key as funder). `signer-set` counts the template signers (2, or
  1 for Shield). The account rules read the payer as the forced writable signer. 86 rules.
- src/spend.rs: the group key is an owner signer other than the payer, so a dummy output may
  always name it (AssertDummyTags takes the owner signers without the payer). It was a
  participant only when a real output paid it.
- src/fee.rs (new): the fee key. It signs only after `approve` accepted the exact bytes and only
  when it is the payer that the pins name. src/sign.rs makes `approved` visible to it. src/wasm.rs
  exports sol_fee_key, sol_fee_sign, sol_fee_verify (the key part: see the next note).
  src/roles.rs no longer returns the pins (a pin now holds the payer of a proposal).
- tests: tests/fee_payer.rs and tests/fee_key.rs (new); every other changed test file moves to
  the new template (the P5 messages that the group paid are now refused by the payer rules, and
  the P6 compile test compares with the sponsor layout of the same instructions). The change tag
  of a spend is inline: with a sponsor the SDK writes the group key inline (account 0 is the payer).
- vectors: vectors/ts and vectors/ts2 are made again by the generators of the P3 crate with one
  change (a sponsor key is the fee payer, the TS SDK at c232da1b); vectors/smoke is made again by
  examples/gen_vectors.rs (the generator of the P3 crate, with the new rules, and two new cases,
  payer-is-group and group-debit). Run `cargo run --example gen_vectors`, `sh build.sh`, then the
  checks in the header of build.sh.
- tools/mutate_sol.py: 15 mutation cases for the new rules and template lines (all killed by
  their named test), and the two new test files in its list.
- Live check on Devnet, 16 October 2026 (no state change): a sponsor that holds no input pays and
  a registered key signs as owner signer. The deployed pool accepts it in a simulation with the
  signatures checked (140,236 compute units), and refuses the same proof with no owner signer, with
  the owner as payer and with the two keys swapped (error 7008). The accounts of the template
  `transact` equal those that the SDK lists, in the same order and with the same flags. The
  messages of the wasm for the nonce account (300 compute units) and for Add SOL (37,910) also run
  in a simulation, and the template `register` has the accounts and the data of the SDK builder
