The program design (16 October 2026, not signed by a verifier; ZOLANA.md 7.2, TICKETS.md SOL-36
condition 2). The funds of a group belong to the PDA of the approvals program (version 2 on
Devnet), and the group key signs the 32-byte digest of an approval in place of a message. The beta
signs a nonce message only for the move of its funds to the PDA:
- src/program.rs (new): the PDA `["multisig", group key]`, the proposal address `[
  "proposed_transaction", group key, commitment]` (version 2, one function), the cancellation
  address, the body, the digest SHA-256("Zigs_SolApproval_v1" || Devnet genesis || program id ||
  proposal || body), the Ed25519 instruction data, the commitment SHA-256(private_tx_hash ||
  external-data hash) and the recompute of private_tx_hash.
- src/pay.rs (new): `approve_pay` runs the transact rules and every Outputs, Legs and Ciphertexts
  rule on the first proof of a payment, through a Transfer with no nonce and a message whose only
  instruction is the transact (so only inline owner tags pass), recomputes private_tx_hash from the
  snapshot inputs, the plan outputs and the root seed, and checks the body and the proposal account
  that the device read (`Seen`), and one body per commitment.
- src/beta.rs (new): which intents each key signs. The group key: CreateNonce and a nonce Transfer
  that pays its inputs whole to the PDA address of the group (`migration-payee`). The fee key:
  those, Shield (to the PDA identity), Propose and Execute (the approval verifies under the group
  key over the digest of the body that the fresh transact data gives). Nothing signs register, a
  withdrawal or a nonce cancel (`intent-retired`). `approve_payment` is the approval of a payment.
- src/intent.rs: `Intent::Program` with Propose (tag 6), Execute (7) and Approve (8), and `Pay`.
  src/plan.rs: a payment proposal carries the transact data of its first proof.
- src/pins.rs: a fifth pin, the nullifier_pk of the PDA identity (161 bytes on the wire). The PDA
  derives from the group key. `for_pda` gives the pins of the PDA identity, and `multisig` keeps the
  group key. src/check.rs, src/template.rs: the payer is never the group key either.
- src/template.rs: the create message (the payer funds the proposal account) and the execute
  message (the Ed25519 instruction just before `execute`, the transact accounts, the owner PDA as a
  readonly account, last). Caps: 7,832 and 151,437 compute units (SOL-35) plus 50 percent.
- src/rule.rs: 13 rules (99 rules), the groups Program and Policy. `execute-inputs`: a payment
  spends at most 18 inputs, the most that one execute of the program carries (review R7). src/rules_ix.rs: the approvals
  program and the Ed25519 program in their intents only, and the execute data.
- src/approve.rs: `pin_violations` is visible to pay.rs. No rule of approve.rs changed.
- src/roles.rs: the PDA identity (option D: HKDF-SHA256 over solSeed with the info
  "zigs-sol/pda-nullifier-secret/v1" || PDA, 31 bytes; address tag 2). `roles` is unchanged.
- src/sign.rs: `approval_share` signs the digest of a payment and nothing else; `sign_share` runs
  the group policy. src/fee.rs: the fee policy. src/wasm.rs: check_payment, sol_approval_share,
  sol_approval_digest, sol_pda_roles; check_message runs the fee policy; compile_message compiles
  Shield, Propose and Execute for the PDA identity (`beta::identity`).
- tests: program.rs (the landed approvals of tracks dmain and emain), payment.rs, pay_vectors.rs
  (new); tests/common/fixture.rs builds the move to the PDA and payments of the PDA identity; every
  test that the policy refuses names the policy rule and keeps its own rule; tests/roles.rs checks
  the PDA identity against Node and the SDK, and (ignored, SOL35_SEED_FILE) against the landed
  option D deposit of the spike.
- vectors: program/landed.json (public chain data of the spike), pay/*.json
  (solspike/tools/payment_vectors.mjs, the TS SDK at c232da1b), roles.json (the PDA identity of
  each seed), smoke (examples/gen_vectors.rs again, with the case migration).
- tools/mutate_sol.py: 46 cases for the program design, all killed by their named test, and the
  three new test files in its list.

