Withdrawals to a public address (SOL-32, 17 October 2026, not signed by a verifier; ZOLANA.md 5.1,
step 7). Program version 5 takes SOL withdrawal legs:
- src/intent.rs: `Pay` has `payee: Payee`, a shielded address or a public key. A public payee pays
  SOL only. Tags 9, 10 and 11 are Propose, Approve and Execute of a withdrawal (Execute carries the
  recipient); tags 6 to 8 keep their bytes. The nonce-era tag 4 stays retired.
- src/program.rs: `commitment` and `external_data_hash` take the settlements of the legs (the SOL
  interface, then the recipient), hashed after the prefix as the pool does. `max_execute_inputs`:
  two inputs fewer per leg (16 with one leg).
- src/pay.rs: a withdrawal runs the rules of the nonce-era Withdrawal on the first proof (one leg
  of the amount, no payee output), and the verdict echoes the recipient of the intent. New rules
  `withdrawal-recipient` (no account of the pool, the program or the group) and `recipient-account`
  (a System account or none, not executable, at least the rent-exempt minimum after the payment),
  101 rules. `Chain` carries what the device read: the proposal account and the recipient account.
- src/template.rs, src/beta.rs: the execute of a withdrawal lists the SOL interface and the
  recipient after the owner PDA, both writable, and its approval check uses the same settlements.
- src/sign.rs, src/wasm.rs: `check_payment` and `sol_approval_share` take `chain` (`Chain::encode`)
  in place of `seen`. src/rule.rs: the texts of `execute-inputs` and `intent-retired`.
- tests: payment.rs (the withdrawal cases), pay_vectors.rs and vectors/pay/withdraw-change.json
  (the SDK `messageHash` of a withdrawal, solspike/tools/payment_vectors.mjs), fixture.rs.
- tools/mutate_sol.py: 124 cases, all killed by their named test.
- QA round 1: `withdrawal-recipient` also bans the CPI authority of the pool (`Pins::cpi_authority`,
  src/consts.rs `SEED_CPI_AUTHORITY`) and the nullifier PDAs of the inputs. `approve_pay` takes a
  `Read`: the proposer in `check_payment` must give the recipient account too; only the `create`
  message, checked after it, skips the read. 127 cases.
- QA round 2: tests of the nullifier PDA of a second input and of the `create` message of a
  withdrawal; the comment of `recipient_account_violation` says what the rule holds. 129 cases.

Cancel of an expired proposal (SOL-52, 18 October 2026, not signed by a verifier). The fee key
signs one more message alone. Program version 5 is not changed.
- src/intent.rs: `Program::Cancel` (tag 12: commitment, expiry, blockhash). Tag 13 is no intent:
  this app writes no cancellation record, so it has no close. src/consts.rs: `MS_CANCEL`.
- src/template.rs: `cancel` has the body of `body_of` (the payer is the rent recipient), the data
  `[2]` and five accounts: payer, proposal, record, payer, System Program. It carries no abort
  authority, so the program refuses it before the expiry (`NotAbortAuthority`, 6017): the program
  enforces the expiry, the fee key can never cancel a live proposal, and the checker has no clock
  rule. A sixth account (the payer as authority) fails `account-count`.
- src/beta.rs, src/rules_ix.rs: only a fee key signs it, and the approvals program runs only the
  tag 2. Compute units (LiteSVM, version 5): `cancel` after the expiry costs 1,224 whatever the
  bump (it reads no record address): the largest of 400 random proposals, with the record or the
  proposal address funded or not. The floor is 1,224 and the cap 1,836. tests/payment.rs: 15 tests.
- Cap of `create`: `find_program_address` costs 1,500 per bump try, for the proposal address and
  for the owner PDA, so `create` costs 2,062 + 1,500 x tries (LiteSVM), and up to 2,283 more if
  the address is funded. `CU_FLOOR_PROPOSE` is 38,062 (24 tries) and `CU_CAP_PROPOSE` 57,093
  (were 7,832 and 11,748: 4 tries). The owner PDA tries are fixed for a group: a group that needs
  k tries exceeds the floor with a chance of 2^-(24-k) per proposal. The cap leaves room for about
  35 tries with a funded address. No vector or message held the old values. `Approve` has no
  message and shares the limits.

